# Build context for the ITK service image.

# Local environment / editor / VCS
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.log
**/.git
**/.github
**/.gitignore
**/.vscode
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/bin

# Present in the repo, not used by the service:
#   tests/     — CI runs pytest on the host (.github/workflows/ci.yml), never
#                inside this image.
#   scripts/   — each SDK's run_itk.sh runs process_results.py on the host
#                from its own a2a-itk clone, not in the container.
#   dashboard/ — deployed to GitHub Pages by its own workflow.
tests
scripts
dashboard

# Developer tooling, not runtime. pyproto/ is committed, so the image never
# regenerates it.
build_protos.sh
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Deliberately INCLUDED — each of these is easy to mistake for dead weight:
#   uv.lock    — `uv sync --frozen` reproduces exactly what CI resolved.
#   README.md  — pyproject.toml declares `readme = "README.md"`; hatchling
#                fails the build without it. It is a build input, not docs
#                shipping by accident.
#   protos/    — codegen.py symlinks the repo root into fetched rust and java
#                agent dirs so build.rs / protobuf-maven-plugin can read
#                protos/instruction.proto.
#   scenarios/ — the default set for `uv run run_tests.py` inside the image.
